---
description: Depot Conventional Commits
globs: "*"
---
# Depot Conventional Commits

Rule for automatically committing changes made by CursorAI using conventional commits format.

<rule>
name: conventional_commits
description: Automatically commit changes made by CursorAI using conventional commits format
filters:
  - type: event
    pattern: "build_success"
  - type: file_change
    pattern: "*"

actions:
  - type: execute
    command: |
      # First check what changes need to be committed
      git status

      # Format all changed files
      depot-fmt "$DEPOT_ROOT"

      # Add license headers to all changed files
      for FILE in $(git diff --name-only); do
        depot-addlicense "$FILE"
      done

      # Extract the change type and scope from the changes
      CHANGE_TYPE=""
      case "$CHANGE_DESCRIPTION" in
        *"add"*|*"create"*|*"implement"*) CHANGE_TYPE="feat";;
        *"fix"*|*"correct"*|*"resolve"*) CHANGE_TYPE="fix";;
        *"refactor"*|*"restructure"*) CHANGE_TYPE="refactor";;
        *"test"*) CHANGE_TYPE="test";;
        *"doc"*|*"comment"*) CHANGE_TYPE="docs";;
        *"style"*|*"format"*) CHANGE_TYPE="style";;
        *"perf"*|*"optimize"*) CHANGE_TYPE="perf";;
        *) CHANGE_TYPE="chore";;
      esac

      # Extract scope from file path
      SCOPE=$(dirname "$FILE" | tr '/' '-')

      # Stage and commit the changes
      git add -u  # Stage all tracked, modified files
      git add "$FILE"  # Stage any new files
      git commit -m "$CHANGE_TYPE($SCOPE): $CHANGE_DESCRIPTION"

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow these steps when committing changes:

      1. Always check what needs to be committed first:
         ```bash
         git status
         ```
         This will show:
         - Changes staged for commit
         - Changes not staged for commit
         - Untracked files

      2. Format code and add license headers:
         ```bash
         # Format all files in the depot
         depot-fmt "$DEPOT_ROOT"

         # Add license headers to changed files
         for FILE in $(git diff --name-only); do
           depot-addlicense "$FILE"
         done
         ```

      3. Group related changes into logical commits
         - Each commit should represent one logical change
         - Multiple files can be included if they're part of the same change
         - Unrelated changes should be in separate commits

      4. Use conventional commits format:
         ```
         <type>(<scope>): <description>
         ```

      Types:
      - feat: A new feature
      - fix: A bug fix
      - docs: Documentation only changes
      - style: Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code
      - refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
      - perf: A code change that improves performance
      - test: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
      - chore: Changes to the build process or auxiliary tools

      The scope should be derived from the file path or affected component.
      The description should be clear and concise, written in imperative mood.

examples:
  - input: |
      # Check current changes
      $ git status
      Changes not staged for commit:
        modified:   src/auth/login.ts

      # After determining it's a new feature
      CHANGE_DESCRIPTION="add user authentication function"
      FILE="src/auth/login.ts"
    output: |
      # Format all files
      depot-fmt "$DEPOT_ROOT"

      # Add license headers to changed files
      depot-addlicense src/auth/login.ts

      # Commit with conventional format
      git add src/auth/login.ts
      git commit -m "feat(src-auth): add user authentication function"

  - input: |
      # Check current changes
      $ git status
      Changes not staged for commit:
        modified:   lib/utils/date.js
        modified:   lib/utils/time.js

      # After determining it's a bug fix affecting multiple files
      CHANGE_DESCRIPTION="fix incorrect date parsing"
      FILES="lib/utils/date.js lib/utils/time.js"
    output: |
      # Format all files
      depot-fmt "$DEPOT_ROOT"

      # Add license headers to all changed files
      depot-addlicense lib/utils/date.js lib/utils/time.js

      # Commit related changes together
      git add lib/utils/date.js lib/utils/time.js
      git commit -m "fix(lib-utils): fix incorrect date parsing"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.2
</rule>

